Source Reward Any husk kill <code>1 + BonusPearls</code> pearls (tower omen, ledger heirloom, Greed creed) Chest <code>10 + pilgrimages × 2</code> pearls, +5 wood, +4 stone Treasure chest the same, plus +1 key, and no omen choice Non-treasure chest the same, then an omen offer of two unowned cards Merchant heirloom 25 pearls, attire 30 pearls, potion 18, key 10, heal 30 hp for 15 Cursed altar +1 key, +25 pearls, −20 health Warden (first kill) 8 / 12 / 16 devotion Every omen already owned the omen offer converts to +25 pearls <pre><code>public void OpenChest()
{
    if (!ChestReady) return;
    ...
    int depth = HarvestState.Data.pilgrimages;
    int pearls = 10 + depth * 2;
    HarvestState.Data.pearls += pearls;
    HarvestState.Data.wood += 5;
    HarvestState.Data.stone += 4;
    ...
    if (CurrentRoomType == RoomType.Treasure) { keys++; ... return; }

    boot.ShowOmenMenu(OpenExit);
}
</code></pre>

Landmark Position (x, z) What it does Harvest Altar <code>0, 1.5</code> Ceremony menu, 30 s cooldown, radius 3.2 Temple statue <code>0, 8</code> Backdrop; blocks building placement Pilgrimage portal <code>8.2, -4.5</code> Opens the pilgrimage map (act select) The Oracle <code>4, 3.8</code> Nine-step hint dialogue and campaign progress The Sovereign (player) <code>0, -3</code> Spawn point; returns here after death Gathering nodes random 10 trees, 8 rocks, three hits each <p>Movement is clamped to <code>hubBounds</code>, computed once as <code>(WorldWidth / 2 - 1, WorldHeight / 2 - 1)</code> — about <code>±19</code> on x and <code>±14</code> on z. The camera follows the player, clamped a little tighter still (<code>WorldWidth / 2 - 6</code>). Building placement uses its own tighter box (<code>±17.5</code> by <code>±12.5</code>).</p> <pre><code>void BuildHarvestAltar()
{
    var altarSprite = Resources.Load&lt;Sprite&gt;("Art/World/altar");
    Vector3 altarPos = Stage3D.P(0f, 1.5f);
    var altarGo = Stage3D.CreateBillboard(hubRoot.transform, "HarvestAltar", altarSprite, altarPos,
        2.6f, Color.white, Stage3D.SortOrder(altarPos));
    Stage3D.CreateShadow(hubRoot.transform, altarGo.transform, 1.3f);

    HarvestAltarRef = altarGo.AddComponent&lt;HarvestAltar&gt;();
}
</code></pre>

Input Binding Method Slot F5 <code>Bindings.Action.Save</code> (default <code>Key.F5</code>) <code>SaveGame()</code> <code>ActiveSlot</code> F9 <code>Bindings.Action.Load</code> (default <code>Key.F9</code>) <code>LoadGame()</code> <code>ActiveSlot</code> — <code>Autosave()</code> <code>Save(AutosaveSlot)</code> 0 <p>Both hotkeys go through <code>Bindings.Pressed</code>, so rebinding them in Settings → Gameplay → Rebind keys changes the save keys too. They are ignored while <code>HarvestGame.InputLocked</code> is set or while a menu is open, because <code>Update</code> returns before reaching them.</p> <p><code>Autosave()</code> respects the autosave preference, and the shipped game has exactly one call site for it:</p> <pre><code>public static void Autosave()
{
    if (!Preferences.Autosave) return;
    Save(AutosaveSlot);
}
// HarvestGame.ExitExpedition
if (loot) HarvestSaveSystem.Autosave();
</code></pre> <p>So the autosave slot is refreshed when an expedition ends successfully — not on day change, not on quest completion, not on quit. <code>Preferences.Autosave</code> defaults to <code>true</code> and is toggled in Settings → More (<code>choth_settings_autosave</code>).</p>

Member Returns Description <code>Locale</code> <code>string</code> Active locale id, <code>"en"</code> until <code>SetLocale</code> <code>Get(string key, string fallback = null)</code> <code>string</code> Table value, else <code>fallback</code>, else the key itself <code>Format(string key, string fallback, params object[] args)</code> <code>string</code> <code>Get</code> then <code>string.Format</code>; a broken template returns unformatted text <code>KeyCount</code> <code>int</code> Entries loaded for the active locale <code>SetLocale(string next)</code> <code>void</code> Switches locale, clears the cache, reloads on next lookup <p>The table is <code>Resources/Localization/&lt;locale&gt;.json</code>, loaded once and cached until the locale changes. A missing file leaves the table empty rather than throwing, so every string falls back to its in-code default. The file shape is fixed by <code>JsonUtility</code>:</p> <pre><code>{
  "entries": [
    { "key": "title.name", "value": "CHOSEN OF THE HARVEST" }
  ]
}
</code></pre> <p><code>Lexicon.Get</code> is also used with a literal default at the call site, which is why code reads like <code>Lexicon.Get("dungeon.locked", "The door is locked …")</code> — that second argument is the fallback, not a translation.</p> <p>Duplicate keys: last one wins</p> <p><code>menu.assign.title</code> is defined twice in <code>en.json</code> — once as <code>ASSIGN</code> and later as <code>ASSIGN {0}</code>. The loader assigns <code>Values[key] = value</code> in file order, so the later entry replaces the earlier one. Remove the first entry when you translate.</p> <p>Where the locale is chosen</p> <p><code>Preferences.Language</code> is stored in PlayerPrefs as <code>choth_settings_language</code>. Settings page 2 cycles English ⇄ Pseudo, and <code>HarvestGame</code> applies it through <code>Lexicon.SetLocale</code> when the game starts.</p>
